WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.740
Could Elvis be destined for the deserts&nbsp;
of Arrakis? Just ask Austin Butler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.860
whose iconic drawl doesn't seem&nbsp;
to be going anywhere anytime soon.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.900
"But in the end you gotta listen to yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.780
So I want you to know those New York&nbsp;
people ain’t gonna change me none."

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.940
The Golden Globes returned on January&nbsp;
10th to celebrate the 80th anniversary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.260
of the all-encompassing entertainment award&nbsp;
ceremony. This year, the Golden Globes awarded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.460
well-deserved television and film nominees such&nbsp;
as the side-splitting gem Abbott Elementary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.300
legendary Black Panther: Wakanda&nbsp;
Forever actress Angela Bassett,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.380
and the dazzling star Austin Butler for his&nbsp;
show-stopping performance as Elvis Presley.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.100
"Mumbling incoherently to the&nbsp;
audience was a good show?"&nbsp;

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.500
"Colonel, I know when I've excited an audience."

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.800
Butler's faithful portrayal of&nbsp;
Elvis skyrocketed the success of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.820
Baz Luhrmann's biopic with a near perfect&nbsp;
audience score on Rotten Tomatoes. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.320
launched the film to an impressive global&nbsp;
box office take of $287 million among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.220
the summer's competitive slate. With one&nbsp;
award already under his glistening belt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.940
it's safe to say he now has an even better&nbsp;
chance of securing the Oscar in March.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.540
"Everything’s happening to me so&nbsp;
fast in the last year and a half,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.560
I’m all mixed up, you know, I can’t keep&nbsp;
up with everything that’s happening."

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.660
When Butler came onstage to receive his award for&nbsp;
Elvis, his voice sounded astonishingly similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:20.040
the beloved musician, using a rich baritone&nbsp;
and slight twang that's reminiscent of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.420
film portrayal. As it turns out, the actor has&nbsp;
some surprising thoughts about that resemblance.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.500
Speaking with People magazine, Butler broke&nbsp;
down the parallels between himself and Elvis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.920
and offered some explanation as to&nbsp;
why they might sound similar. He even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.680
detailedk the meaningful relationship&nbsp;
he shares with the Presley family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:38.160
which culminated in his authentic&nbsp;
representation of the iconic star.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.580
Backstage at the bustling award show,&nbsp;
Butler told reporters that he doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.480
hear Elvis in his own voice. However, he&nbsp;
didn't shoot down the possibility that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:48.540
the performance has stayed with him,&nbsp;
given how long he spent playing Elvis.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.020
"I had three years where that&nbsp;
was my only focus in life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.680
so I'm sure that there's just pieces of my&nbsp;
DNA that will always be linked in that way."

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.340
Butler has been open about his special&nbsp;
connection with Elvis that led him to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.240
part. The acclaimed actor also expressed&nbsp;
his gratitude and thanked the Presley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.260
family for their blessing and encouragement.
All you have to do is comb through social media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.640
to find a ton of comments from fans that point out&nbsp;
how different Austin Butler's voice has been since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:16.320
Elvis. And in fact, his recent interviews aren't&nbsp;
the first time the actor referenced it. Butler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:21.660
previously addressed the vocal similarity on his&nbsp;
Saturday Night Live debut in December 2022. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.620
his opening monologue, he spoke about how people&nbsp;
have been talking about his alleged new voice.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:31.380
"That it got deeper, more Elvis-y. But that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.620
not true. I've always sounded&nbsp;
like this, and I can prove it."

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.880
He then transitioned to an interview clip&nbsp;
from 10 years ago — with one small change.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:42.360
"How excited are you to be&nbsp;
Sebastian on The Carrie Diaries?"&nbsp;

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.360
"I'm really excited. It's been&nbsp;
a great experience so far."

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.140
It's clear he's willing to have some fun with&nbsp;
his fame, and any criticism that may come his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.820
way. But will Austin Butler's voice ever go&nbsp;
back to the way it was? Only time will tell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.240
but one thing is for certain: With&nbsp;
Butler slated for a role in Dune:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.620
Part 2, it sure would be interesting to see&nbsp;
an Elvis impersonator turn up on Arrakis.

